1
00:01:47,079 --> 00:01:47,680
Xiaozhou,

2
00:01:48,319 --> 00:01:50,239
go get me a pack of cigarettes,

3
00:01:50,239 --> 00:01:51,480
and a lighter, too.

4
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:07,359
Hey, boss.

5
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:08,319
What can I get you?

6
00:02:08,319 --> 00:02:08,879
Got any cigarettes?

7
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:47,439
All right, take care.

8
00:02:53,199 --> 00:02:54,280
Okay, thanks.

9
00:03:06,039 --> 00:03:07,199
Hello. Welcome.

10
00:03:07,439 --> 00:03:07,919
Check, please.

11
00:03:08,719 --> 00:03:10,280
Someone just opened a black card for you

12
00:03:10,439 --> 00:03:11,520
and loaded 50,000 onto it.

13
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:18,560
Please come again.

14
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:31,000
Doctors always make things sound terrifying.

15
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:32,560
It's nothing serious.

16
00:04:32,639 --> 00:04:33,800
If it were really that bad,

17
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:35,199
he wouldn't dare let you travel so far

18
00:04:35,199 --> 00:04:36,160
to see a doctor out of town.

19
00:04:36,839 --> 00:04:38,360
He'd have admitted you to the hospital.

20
00:04:38,839 --> 00:04:40,000
Why don't we go to Beijing?

21
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:42,399
As long as your secretary stays quiet,

22
00:04:42,399 --> 00:04:43,279
and your driver does too,

23
00:04:43,279 --> 00:04:44,439
who's ever going to find out?

24
00:04:44,839 --> 00:04:47,160
It'll be fine. Don't worry.

25
00:05:03,839 --> 00:05:05,279
If I were afraid you'd call the police,

26
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:07,240
I wouldn't be sitting here.

27
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:08,439
As for you,

28
00:05:09,079 --> 00:05:10,560
you wouldn't be dismissed, of course.

29
00:05:11,600 --> 00:05:14,319
But you'd lose your deputy directorship.

30
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:15,759
The Economic Committee,

31
00:05:15,759 --> 00:05:17,079
the Academic Research Association,

32
00:05:17,079 --> 00:05:18,600
Provincial Government Special Advisor...

33
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:21,079
all of those positions would be affected.

34
00:05:21,519 --> 00:05:22,800
And as for your husband,

35
00:05:22,879 --> 00:05:24,639
he already has health issues.

36
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:27,600
If his wife gets linked to espionage,

37
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:29,600
his promising political career

38
00:05:29,839 --> 00:05:31,120
would end right there.

39
00:05:32,560 --> 00:05:33,399
Then there's that child at home,

40
00:05:33,399 --> 00:05:35,279
the one who will never grow up.

41
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,279
They still have a long road ahead.

42
00:05:38,120 --> 00:05:39,160
If they inadvertently

43
00:05:39,160 --> 00:05:40,519
got mixed up with spies,

44
00:05:41,639 --> 00:05:43,079
you wouldn't want anything to go wrong.

45
00:06:22,319 --> 00:06:24,399
Once you work at Lin Kanshan's company,

46
00:06:24,399 --> 00:06:25,720
we won't be able to

47
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:26,800
meet as often as we do now.

48
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:29,519
Do you remember our detailed protocol?

49
00:06:30,199 --> 00:06:31,399
Unless it's an emergency,

50
00:06:31,399 --> 00:06:32,519
we'll meet on the first of every month.

51
00:07:55,519 --> 00:07:56,759
Hello, Professor Pan.

52
00:08:12,639 --> 00:08:13,240
Come in.

53
00:08:16,759 --> 00:08:17,439
President.

54
00:08:18,279 --> 00:08:19,160
Professor Pan.

55
00:08:19,160 --> 00:08:20,399
Come, please have a seat.

56
00:08:20,839 --> 00:08:23,240
First draft. Headings are preliminary.

57
00:08:23,319 --> 00:08:24,720
Whatever doesn't work,

58
00:08:24,720 --> 00:08:25,839
feel free to change it.

59
00:08:26,240 --> 00:08:26,959
That was fast.

60
00:08:29,160 --> 00:08:30,920
Both quick and well done.

61
00:08:32,039 --> 00:08:33,720
You really are the right person for this.

62
00:08:44,919 --> 00:08:46,000
Severe anxiety.

63
00:08:46,080 --> 00:08:47,080
Lifelong medication.

64
00:08:47,559 --> 00:08:49,559
I'm applying for medical retirement.

65
00:08:53,720 --> 00:08:54,600
Yes.

66
00:08:54,879 --> 00:08:56,879
It's only been a few days.

67
00:08:58,120 --> 00:08:59,960
I didn't feel anything at all.

68
00:09:00,559 --> 00:09:02,039
How was I supposed to know I'm pregnant?

69
00:09:03,799 --> 00:09:05,360
If not for the physical at school,

70
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:07,360
I was even planning to play ball tomorrow.

71
00:09:09,720 --> 00:09:11,240
You don't need to put him on.

72
00:09:11,600 --> 00:09:13,279
Dad nags more and more these days.

73
00:09:13,279 --> 00:09:14,679
He'll just go on and on.

74
00:09:14,679 --> 00:09:15,960
I don't want to talk to him.

75
00:09:18,120 --> 00:09:19,440
Hold on, my phone's dying.

76
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:20,399
I'll call you from the dorm.

77
00:09:20,399 --> 00:09:21,200
Bye, Mom.

78
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:23,440
If my mom hadn't reminded me,

79
00:09:23,440 --> 00:09:24,519
I would've forgotten.

80
00:09:24,679 --> 00:09:25,360
What?

81
00:09:25,600 --> 00:09:27,440
I don't think we can register it here.

82
00:09:27,759 --> 00:09:29,080
Otherwise, as my belly grows,

83
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:30,759
we'd have to keep running back and forth.

84
00:09:31,799 --> 00:09:32,960
Should we register

85
00:09:32,960 --> 00:09:34,200
at a hospital in Xiamen instead?

86
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:36,559
Yeah.

87
00:09:36,960 --> 00:09:38,600
Staying at school alone isn't good either.

88
00:09:39,080 --> 00:09:43,399
How about I care for you in Xiamen?

89
00:09:45,240 --> 00:09:46,720
Don't you have to work?

90
00:09:46,840 --> 00:09:47,559
Right.

91
00:09:49,440 --> 00:09:51,320
You want to quit to be my full-time nanny?

92
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:53,480
Can I?

93
00:09:53,919 --> 00:09:54,440
No need.

94
00:09:55,639 --> 00:09:57,000
Just stay here.

95
00:09:57,200 --> 00:09:58,120
Don't go back to school.

96
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:01,960
Today is my dad's birthday.

97
00:10:02,080 --> 00:10:02,600
Perfect timing.

98
00:10:03,039 --> 00:10:04,679
I'll head back later and talk to them.

99
00:10:05,759 --> 00:10:06,879
Don't talk to her.

100
00:10:08,720 --> 00:10:10,399
Talking to your mom only makes it worse.

101
00:10:10,879 --> 00:10:11,919
We're better off leaving things as is.

102
00:10:15,279 --> 00:10:16,720
It's not like I'm forcing you.

103
00:10:16,879 --> 00:10:17,799
Besides,

104
00:10:17,799 --> 00:10:19,200
my parents are here too.

105
00:10:19,320 --> 00:10:20,519
What are you afraid of?

106
00:10:37,600 --> 00:10:38,480
This is the place.

107
00:10:39,039 --> 00:10:39,840
I'm heading out then.

108
00:10:48,320 --> 00:10:49,600
Hate to see me go?

109
00:10:52,159 --> 00:10:52,960
You're pregnant.

110
00:10:52,960 --> 00:10:54,000
Don't drink coffee.

111
00:10:55,879 --> 00:10:57,799
I know. I won't drink any.

112
00:10:58,240 --> 00:10:59,320
I'll head back later

113
00:10:59,480 --> 00:11:00,679
and talk things through with Mom and Dad.

114
00:11:01,559 --> 00:11:02,320
No fighting.

115
00:11:03,720 --> 00:11:04,759
Nobody's forcing you.

116
00:11:06,440 --> 00:11:07,600
Remember what I told you.

117
00:11:07,759 --> 00:11:08,519
Okay.

118
00:11:11,759 --> 00:11:12,320
I'm off.

119
00:11:12,799 --> 00:11:13,440
Go ahead.

120
00:11:23,039 --> 00:11:24,679
Hello. Would you like anything to drink?

121
00:11:24,679 --> 00:11:25,559
No, thank you.

122
00:11:25,559 --> 00:11:26,440
All right.

123
00:11:56,360 --> 00:11:57,799
Americano, no milk.

124
00:11:58,080 --> 00:12:01,080
Not as good as that cafe in Barcelona,

125
00:12:01,279 --> 00:12:02,440
but it'll have to do.

126
00:12:02,639 --> 00:12:04,519
No, thanks.

127
00:12:10,799 --> 00:12:12,759
No coffee while pregnant?

128
00:12:15,840 --> 00:12:17,000
He went home.

129
00:12:17,600 --> 00:12:19,320
He'll definitely confront his parents.

130
00:12:20,480 --> 00:12:21,639
Who will give in?

131
00:12:22,399 --> 00:12:24,000
Whether I go back to Xiamen or stay here,

132
00:12:24,440 --> 00:12:25,480
whether he resigns or not...

133
00:12:25,480 --> 00:12:26,840
It's still hard to say.

134
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:30,519
It depends on how much they spoil him.

135
00:12:31,159 --> 00:12:32,840
One is a government official,

136
00:12:33,480 --> 00:12:35,000
the other is a university professor.

137
00:12:35,600 --> 00:12:37,120
What if they don't spoil him?

138
00:12:37,440 --> 00:12:38,639
What if they're strict?

139
00:12:43,480 --> 00:12:44,879
Things are always changing,

140
00:12:45,120 --> 00:12:46,399
and people change too.

141
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:49,000
So we can only take it one step at a time.

142
00:12:51,200 --> 00:12:52,480
Is there anything else you want to say?

143
00:12:56,399 --> 00:12:58,759
Have you fallen in love with him?

144
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:02,960
Are you asking this, or did someone else?

145
00:13:05,200 --> 00:13:07,960
Whether in Spain or on the mainland,

146
00:13:08,759 --> 00:13:10,440
your mission is to cooperate with me.

147
00:13:10,799 --> 00:13:13,600
Page 980 of the Modern Chinese Dictionary.

148
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:14,840
You can look it up.

149
00:13:15,159 --> 00:13:16,679
See what "cooperation" means.

150
00:13:16,679 --> 00:13:17,519
"Working in coordination,

151
00:13:17,519 --> 00:13:18,559
acting jointly."

152
00:13:20,360 --> 00:13:21,720
Cooperation goes both ways.

153
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:23,519
I haven't received any other orders.

154
00:13:26,039 --> 00:13:27,320
I have other orders.

155
00:13:27,720 --> 00:13:29,360
If you're hiding anything,

156
00:13:29,639 --> 00:13:32,159
you'll find out what those orders mean.

157
00:13:35,039 --> 00:13:37,039
The higher-ups said to protect yourself.

158
00:13:37,440 --> 00:13:39,720
I believe that includes your womb.

159
00:13:42,200 --> 00:13:43,360
The higher-ups also said

160
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:46,480
mainlanders drop dead all the time.

161
00:13:46,879 --> 00:13:48,799
If you insist on marrying a mainlander

162
00:13:48,919 --> 00:13:50,600
and end up a widow by accident,

163
00:13:51,240 --> 00:13:52,200
that wouldn't be good either.

164
00:13:55,840 --> 00:13:57,200
You're threatening me.

165
00:14:04,039 --> 00:14:05,759
Once you get on this boat,

166
00:14:06,039 --> 00:14:07,200
there's no getting off.

167
00:14:08,279 --> 00:14:09,679
In any other profession in the world,

168
00:14:09,679 --> 00:14:11,440
you can just walk away.

169
00:14:11,840 --> 00:14:12,840
Not us.

170
00:14:13,639 --> 00:14:15,039
That goes for you, and for me.

171
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:17,039
If I were to quit,

172
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:18,320
would someone in Taipei

173
00:14:18,320 --> 00:14:20,159
pull the plug on my dad at the hospital?

174
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:23,399
What constitutes a threat?

175
00:14:23,679 --> 00:14:24,679
Why don't you teach me?

176
00:14:29,559 --> 00:14:31,759
Have you done what the higher-ups ordered?

177
00:14:32,639 --> 00:14:35,000
Did he smoke the weed today?

178
00:14:47,480 --> 00:14:48,519
Weed is too slow.

179
00:14:49,320 --> 00:14:52,080
Lace it with the stuff under the leaves.

180
00:15:14,080 --> 00:15:16,039
Before the pathology results come in,

181
00:15:16,039 --> 00:15:17,519
stop looking at it over and over.

182
00:15:18,120 --> 00:15:19,919
Like the college entrance exam back then.

183
00:15:20,279 --> 00:15:21,240
No matter how much you worry,

184
00:15:21,240 --> 00:15:22,639
it's already set in stone.

185
00:15:22,759 --> 00:15:25,279
If you fail, then worry about retaking it.

186
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:30,679
I heard Vice Governor Wu's daughter

187
00:15:30,960 --> 00:15:32,279
really likes your son.

188
00:15:33,919 --> 00:15:36,360
Wasn't her daughter studying in the UK?

189
00:15:36,440 --> 00:15:37,600
Graduated so soon?

190
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:38,960
Whether she graduated doesn't matter.

191
00:15:38,960 --> 00:15:40,559
She's already back now.

192
00:15:40,600 --> 00:15:42,200
She just started working at a bank.

193
00:15:42,320 --> 00:15:43,200
A bank is good.

194
00:15:43,399 --> 00:15:44,279
Low-key,

195
00:15:44,399 --> 00:15:45,639
and it suits her personality.

196
00:15:45,879 --> 00:15:47,519
I've met the girl before.

197
00:15:47,600 --> 00:15:49,200
She's sensible and polite.

198
00:15:49,519 --> 00:15:50,440
Very nice.

199
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:52,159
Maybe you're the only one who thinks so.

200
00:15:52,159 --> 00:15:53,879
As long as we think so, that's enough.

201
00:15:54,360 --> 00:15:55,759
I don't care about anything else.

202
00:15:56,080 --> 00:15:58,879
How often does one get married in life?

203
00:15:58,919 --> 00:16:00,000
Matters like this

204
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:01,720
ought to be decided by us parents.

205
00:16:04,039 --> 00:16:07,360
Word is Vice Governor Wu is moving up.

206
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:11,759
Lao Xie,

207
00:16:14,080 --> 00:16:17,120
there's something I need to discuss.

208
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:18,960
Your university president called me.

209
00:16:19,240 --> 00:16:21,440
You can't resign right now.

210
00:16:22,039 --> 00:16:22,960
You must hold on to

211
00:16:22,960 --> 00:16:24,960
the Economic Committee deputy position.

212
00:16:26,679 --> 00:16:28,080
Giving lectures to the governor

213
00:16:28,080 --> 00:16:29,320
is very important.

214
00:16:29,840 --> 00:16:31,120
Just as important to me.

215
00:16:31,399 --> 00:16:32,240
But...

216
00:16:33,320 --> 00:16:34,159
I'm home.

217
00:16:36,159 --> 00:16:37,080
Our son is back.

218
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:41,679
We agreed on twelve.

219
00:16:41,840 --> 00:16:43,799
It's 11:59 now.

220
00:16:43,799 --> 00:16:44,679
I'm not late.

221
00:16:48,279 --> 00:16:49,960
Your mom was just worried you'd be hungry.

222
00:16:50,960 --> 00:16:52,320
Come on, wash your hands and let's eat.

223
00:16:53,919 --> 00:16:55,159
It's really rare

224
00:16:55,679 --> 00:16:57,240
for all of us to get together for a meal.

225
00:16:57,519 --> 00:16:59,679
Not too much, just three small cups each.

226
00:17:00,200 --> 00:17:00,759
Here.

227
00:17:00,759 --> 00:17:02,360
You're drinking too?

228
00:17:02,879 --> 00:17:03,960
Just a little.

229
00:17:06,119 --> 00:17:06,640
Son.

230
00:17:06,839 --> 00:17:07,640
I drove.

231
00:17:08,119 --> 00:17:09,960
I'm busy this afternoon, so no drinks.

232
00:17:09,960 --> 00:17:10,880
Just take a sip.

233
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:12,440
What plans do you have this afternoon?

234
00:17:15,680 --> 00:17:16,200
Nothing.

235
00:17:17,319 --> 00:17:19,079
Do you or don't you?

236
00:17:21,079 --> 00:17:22,440
It's your dad's birthday.

237
00:17:22,559 --> 00:17:24,160
He hasn't even picked up his chopsticks.

238
00:17:33,920 --> 00:17:34,599
Xiaoyu,

239
00:17:35,400 --> 00:17:36,519
when will dinner be ready?

240
00:17:36,519 --> 00:17:37,079
I'm starving.

241
00:17:37,079 --> 00:17:38,079
Soon, soon. Almost ready.

242
00:17:40,039 --> 00:17:42,599
I called your workplace this morning.

243
00:17:42,599 --> 00:17:44,119
They said you took time off.

244
00:17:44,160 --> 00:17:45,519
The reason was to visit the hospital.

245
00:17:46,720 --> 00:17:47,680
What happened to you?

246
00:17:48,160 --> 00:17:49,720
Must we discuss this before dinner?

247
00:17:52,440 --> 00:17:54,039
If it's unpleasant,

248
00:17:54,039 --> 00:17:55,799
it won't sound any better later.

249
00:17:55,839 --> 00:17:57,119
What do you want to say?

250
00:18:01,079 --> 00:18:02,200
Huang Ziyan is pregnant.

251
00:18:03,480 --> 00:18:05,519
We went to the hospital to register today.

252
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:11,079
Who is Huang Ziyan?

253
00:18:11,640 --> 00:18:12,640
Have you heard of her?

254
00:18:15,680 --> 00:18:17,720
I don't have time for a stranger.

255
00:18:18,799 --> 00:18:20,519
She's my girlfriend.

256
00:18:20,920 --> 00:18:21,920
My fiancée.

257
00:18:22,480 --> 00:18:23,880
The mother of my child.

258
00:18:28,119 --> 00:18:29,519
Say that again.

259
00:18:31,319 --> 00:18:32,480
She's my girlfriend.

260
00:18:32,480 --> 00:18:34,519
My fiancée. The mother of my child.

261
00:18:39,960 --> 00:18:40,920
That's enough, Xiaozhou.

262
00:18:41,519 --> 00:18:43,000
There's something I need to tell you.

263
00:18:43,720 --> 00:18:44,759
Come with me for a moment.

264
00:18:45,519 --> 00:18:46,200
Let's go.

265
00:18:51,680 --> 00:18:53,039
Xiaozhou. Xiaozhou.

266
00:18:53,079 --> 00:18:53,920
Get in.

267
00:18:54,079 --> 00:18:54,519
Get inside.

268
00:18:54,519 --> 00:18:54,920
Let go of me!

269
00:18:59,799 --> 00:19:00,519
Son.

270
00:19:01,119 --> 00:19:02,880
Dad promises you on his Party integrity,

271
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:05,319
I'm not trying to break you two up.

272
00:19:05,319 --> 00:19:06,920
This has nothing to do with your mother.

273
00:19:07,160 --> 00:19:08,039
However, there are things

274
00:19:08,440 --> 00:19:09,599
that you must know.

275
00:19:12,640 --> 00:19:14,079
That girlfriend of yours...

276
00:19:14,839 --> 00:19:15,799
She's a spy.

277
00:19:17,160 --> 00:19:18,279
She will destroy you,

278
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:19,799
destroy me, destroy your mother,

279
00:19:19,799 --> 00:19:21,480
and ruin our entire family.

280
00:19:21,480 --> 00:19:22,920
She is a spy from Taiwan, China.

281
00:19:24,920 --> 00:19:25,799
The child isn't.

282
00:19:25,799 --> 00:19:27,759
Are you crazy? What are you thinking?

283
00:19:27,759 --> 00:19:28,920
Is she threatening you?

284
00:19:30,960 --> 00:19:32,680
Son, don't be a fool.

285
00:19:32,680 --> 00:19:33,640
You're not in Europe anymore.

286
00:19:33,640 --> 00:19:35,039
You are in your own home.

287
00:19:35,039 --> 00:19:36,279
Everyone standing behind you can help you.

288
00:19:36,279 --> 00:19:37,319
What are you afraid of?

289
00:19:39,759 --> 00:19:40,799
I'm afraid of you.

290
00:19:42,400 --> 00:19:43,480
I'm afraid of Mom.

291
00:19:44,720 --> 00:19:45,920
Except for the two of you,

292
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:47,680
I'm not afraid of anyone.

293
00:19:51,799 --> 00:19:52,680
Son.

294
00:19:53,119 --> 00:19:54,319
Son, listen to me.

295
00:19:55,720 --> 00:19:57,160
I don't care what your mother thinks,

296
00:19:57,319 --> 00:19:58,920
nor do I care what she will do.

297
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:01,279
I hoped you'd find a matching family,

298
00:20:01,279 --> 00:20:03,640
but ultimately, whoever you marry,

299
00:20:03,640 --> 00:20:04,880
as long as it makes you happy,

300
00:20:04,880 --> 00:20:06,119
Dad doesn't care about anything else.

301
00:20:06,400 --> 00:20:06,960
Really.

302
00:20:11,359 --> 00:20:13,200
Dad hasn't been in good health lately,

303
00:20:14,240 --> 00:20:16,599
and I might have to step down soon.

304
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:18,279
I will only have you left.

305
00:20:21,839 --> 00:20:22,640
Are you done?

306
00:20:25,319 --> 00:20:26,079
Xiaozhou.

307
00:20:28,880 --> 00:20:30,359
Back when you were in high school,

308
00:20:30,400 --> 00:20:31,480
you were disobedient, too.

309
00:20:32,359 --> 00:20:33,400
You ran away from home,

310
00:20:33,920 --> 00:20:35,200
and even stayed out all night.

311
00:20:35,200 --> 00:20:36,720
Dad never held any of that against you.

312
00:20:36,960 --> 00:20:38,920
But when you tried to hit your mom,

313
00:20:38,960 --> 00:20:40,319
that was something I could never allow.

314
00:20:41,039 --> 00:20:41,680
Son.

315
00:20:42,119 --> 00:20:43,759
In life, there are boundaries

316
00:20:43,880 --> 00:20:45,519
you must never cross.

317
00:20:45,519 --> 00:20:46,920
Once the bottom line is crossed,

318
00:20:46,920 --> 00:20:48,079
everything is ruined.

319
00:20:48,960 --> 00:20:50,119
Just like you right now.

320
00:20:50,279 --> 00:20:52,519
Dad will never let anyone hurt you.

321
00:20:52,519 --> 00:20:54,119
Do you understand what Dad means?

322
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:57,480
Is this Huang Ziyan?

323
00:20:57,839 --> 00:20:59,400
I am Xie Xiaozhou's mother.

324
00:20:59,640 --> 00:21:01,319
I am officially warning you:

325
00:21:01,480 --> 00:21:03,480
from this very moment,

326
00:21:03,519 --> 00:21:04,960
stop calling him.

327
00:21:04,960 --> 00:21:06,440
It's over between you two.

328
00:21:06,599 --> 00:21:08,720
I don't care what hidden conspiracies

329
00:21:08,720 --> 00:21:09,400
or motives you have.

330
00:21:09,559 --> 00:21:10,359
Mark my words:

331
00:21:10,359 --> 00:21:11,279
if you dare go near him again,

332
00:21:11,279 --> 00:21:12,359
I will make you pay!

333
00:21:12,400 --> 00:21:13,920
I will make you pay!

334
00:21:25,759 --> 00:21:26,640
Satisfied now?

335
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:30,200
Son! Son!

336
00:21:30,680 --> 00:21:31,440
Son!

337
00:21:59,839 --> 00:22:00,920
Actually,

338
00:22:02,440 --> 00:22:04,240
the provincial hospital told me

339
00:22:05,880 --> 00:22:07,480
that polyp of mine doesn't look good.

340
00:22:08,440 --> 00:22:09,720
That woman...

341
00:22:10,759 --> 00:22:12,079
is the devil.

342
00:22:13,640 --> 00:22:15,880
She'll destroy our whole family.

343
00:22:50,519 --> 00:22:52,720
Hello, I'm calling to report a crime.

344
00:22:53,079 --> 00:22:54,359
Someone is using and possessing drugs.

345
00:22:56,559 --> 00:22:57,960
I know his license plate number,

346
00:22:58,720 --> 00:23:00,839
and which residential complex he lives in.

347
00:23:11,279 --> 00:23:12,839
Out of the car! Get out!

348
00:23:12,839 --> 00:23:13,880
Cooperate with the inspection!

349
00:23:14,960 --> 00:23:15,519
Get out!

350
00:23:18,079 --> 00:23:18,880
Get out and cooperate with us!

351
00:23:18,880 --> 00:23:19,599
What's going on?

352
00:23:20,359 --> 00:23:21,079
Pull him out!

353
00:23:21,240 --> 00:23:21,759
Get out of the car!

354
00:23:23,440 --> 00:23:23,799
Don't move!

355
00:23:23,799 --> 00:23:24,799
Don't move! Cooperate with us!

356
00:23:24,799 --> 00:23:26,279
Isn't this Mayor Xie's son, Xie Xiaozhou?

357
00:23:26,279 --> 00:23:27,000
What are you doing?!

358
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:28,240
What the hell are you doing?!

359
00:23:28,359 --> 00:23:29,559
Check his trunk and behind the seats!

360
00:23:29,559 --> 00:23:30,359
Search everywhere thoroughly!

361
00:23:30,359 --> 00:23:31,319
Find where the drugs are hidden!

362
00:23:31,319 --> 00:23:32,720
Bullshit! There are no drugs!

363
00:23:33,200 --> 00:23:34,640
We wouldn't stop you for no reason.

364
00:23:35,039 --> 00:23:35,960
Search it thoroughly!

365
00:23:36,920 --> 00:23:38,039
What's going on? What did he do?

366
00:23:38,039 --> 00:23:40,400
Spill it. Where are the drugs?

367
00:23:44,599 --> 00:23:45,519
That's why I always say...

368
00:23:45,519 --> 00:23:46,720
human relationships...

369
00:23:48,039 --> 00:23:49,200
only come down to four kinds:

370
00:23:49,359 --> 00:23:50,599
repaying favors, seeking revenge,

371
00:23:50,799 --> 00:23:52,000
collecting debts, and paying debts.

372
00:23:52,160 --> 00:23:53,160
If in a family...

373
00:23:53,160 --> 00:23:54,519
you get stuck with two debt collectors,

374
00:23:54,519 --> 00:23:55,440
you're completely finished.

375
00:23:55,680 --> 00:23:56,319
Do you remember that couple

376
00:23:56,319 --> 00:23:57,759
we were staking out in Xiamen?

377
00:23:57,759 --> 00:23:59,000
The husband drove a cab,

378
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:00,319
and the wife was a teacher.

379
00:24:00,319 --> 00:24:01,680
Didn't they fight every single day?

380
00:24:01,759 --> 00:24:03,519
Smashing bowls day in, day out.

381
00:24:03,519 --> 00:24:04,839
Never a single moment of peace.

382
00:24:05,359 --> 00:24:06,559
Whose family fights every day?

383
00:24:06,559 --> 00:24:07,480
Yours, of course.

384
00:24:07,920 --> 00:24:08,839
Our family?

385
00:24:08,920 --> 00:24:11,799
I meant my uncle and aunt fight every day.

386
00:24:12,240 --> 00:24:13,960
They replace the TV every six months.

387
00:24:13,960 --> 00:24:15,240
Sometimes, you know,

388
00:24:15,519 --> 00:24:16,599
if they weren't cut from the same cloth,

389
00:24:17,319 --> 00:24:18,519
they wouldn't end up under one roof.

390
00:24:18,920 --> 00:24:20,319
Strange couple, aren't they?

391
00:24:20,319 --> 00:24:21,640
Bickering ever since they were young,

392
00:24:21,839 --> 00:24:23,440
fighting for life, but never divorcing.

393
00:24:23,920 --> 00:24:25,599
In a situation like that,

394
00:24:26,200 --> 00:24:28,400
the kid suffers the most.

395
00:24:28,400 --> 00:24:29,640
Don't get me started on my cousin.

396
00:24:29,839 --> 00:24:31,680
He grew up cursing my uncle with his mom.

397
00:24:32,119 --> 00:24:33,559
A few times, I almost beat him up.

398
00:24:33,759 --> 00:24:35,240
How is that even a family?

399
00:24:35,720 --> 00:24:36,920
They're like three wild animals.

400
00:24:41,759 --> 00:24:44,119
You just mentioned a family of animals.

401
00:24:44,640 --> 00:24:46,079
What animals are your uncle's family?

402
00:24:48,640 --> 00:24:50,240
What kind? Like wolves and dogs,

403
00:24:50,480 --> 00:24:51,480
snarling and biting each other every day.

404
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:53,559
This email says

405
00:24:53,559 --> 00:24:56,079
Taiwan, China focuses on turning targets.

406
00:24:56,759 --> 00:24:58,279
It also mentions the Three Sparrows.

407
00:24:58,559 --> 00:25:00,319
Lin Kanshan's email says

408
00:25:00,440 --> 00:25:03,240
the Three Sparrows are from the same nest.

409
00:25:04,359 --> 00:25:05,799
They're a family, too:

410
00:25:11,119 --> 00:25:11,960
Xie Xiaozhou,

411
00:25:12,079 --> 00:25:12,839
Pan Xiaoying,

412
00:25:12,960 --> 00:25:13,799
and Xie Fengshi.

413
00:26:00,920 --> 00:26:02,440
I sent the driver to buy water.

414
00:26:02,839 --> 00:26:05,920
I told him you asked me to come over.

415
00:26:08,319 --> 00:26:09,359
I asked you to come over?

416
00:26:10,119 --> 00:26:11,000
What for?

417
00:26:11,480 --> 00:26:12,440
To solve a problem, of course.

418
00:26:13,160 --> 00:26:14,599
A very troublesome one.

419
00:26:17,839 --> 00:26:19,839
The young man from back then has grown up.

420
00:26:20,799 --> 00:26:22,279
He can solve problems now.

421
00:26:22,480 --> 00:26:23,279
Young Boss Lin...

422
00:26:23,400 --> 00:26:25,119
You can't just take the benefits,

423
00:26:25,720 --> 00:26:26,720
and then bite the hand that feeds you.

424
00:26:26,960 --> 00:26:28,279
You shouldn't be like Lee Teng-hui,

425
00:26:29,160 --> 00:26:30,720
that lunatic.

426
00:26:31,079 --> 00:26:33,279
He's been throwing fits on TV lately.

427
00:26:33,519 --> 00:26:34,599
I don't even bother watching him.

428
00:26:34,599 --> 00:26:36,680
I suspect he drank too much fake booze.

429
00:26:41,279 --> 00:26:43,160
Yes, yes. Forget about him.

430
00:26:44,160 --> 00:26:45,200
Drills are drills,

431
00:26:45,319 --> 00:26:46,200
and business is business.

432
00:26:46,480 --> 00:26:47,920
We still need to work together

433
00:26:47,920 --> 00:26:48,799
and focus on development.

434
00:26:48,799 --> 00:26:49,559
Right, right.

435
00:26:50,279 --> 00:26:53,559
We must cooperate no matter what.

436
00:26:54,240 --> 00:26:56,000
Xiaozhou's situation is tricky,

437
00:26:56,440 --> 00:26:57,759
but it's not without a solution.

438
00:26:58,440 --> 00:26:59,720
Swap out the license plate.

439
00:27:00,240 --> 00:27:01,640
Seven days of administrative detention.

440
00:27:01,960 --> 00:27:03,440
He didn't buy the marijuana.

441
00:27:03,720 --> 00:27:04,759
It'll be ruled accidental inhalation.

442
00:27:05,400 --> 00:27:07,079
At most, a failure to identify the drug.

443
00:27:07,559 --> 00:27:09,519
Take leave from work, clear the record,

444
00:27:10,599 --> 00:27:13,200
and act as if this never happened.

445
00:27:21,880 --> 00:27:23,599
I can also make sure your...

446
00:27:23,920 --> 00:27:25,640
grandson's unmarried mother

447
00:27:26,519 --> 00:27:27,720
leaves the mainland for good,

448
00:27:28,119 --> 00:27:29,160
never to return.

449
00:27:34,079 --> 00:27:35,160
This game of chess...

450
00:27:37,160 --> 00:27:39,079
You started playing years ago, didn't you?

451
00:27:40,079 --> 00:27:41,400
One must be candid.

452
00:27:42,440 --> 00:27:44,160
You taught me that when you were mayor.

453
00:27:56,000 --> 00:27:57,519
This is illegal.

454
00:27:58,240 --> 00:27:59,200
So what if it's illegal?

455
00:27:59,759 --> 00:28:00,799
I can't smoke this.

456
00:28:00,799 --> 00:28:01,920
This is marijuana.

457
00:28:02,839 --> 00:28:04,000
Have you ever tried it before?

458
00:28:05,279 --> 00:28:07,480
It's always like this the first time.

459
00:28:08,039 --> 00:28:08,720
I'm so dizzy.

460
00:28:09,400 --> 00:28:11,759
What is this crap? It's awful to smoke.

461
00:28:13,720 --> 00:28:14,920
I know him very well.

462
00:28:15,839 --> 00:28:17,079
We go way back.

463
00:28:18,160 --> 00:28:20,799
Without me, he wouldn't have graduated.

464
00:28:21,440 --> 00:28:23,119
Your brilliant son...

465
00:28:23,640 --> 00:28:25,079
couldn't even write his thesis.

466
00:28:25,359 --> 00:28:26,400
Can you believe that?

467
00:28:30,720 --> 00:28:33,400
Courts rarely admit private recordings.

468
00:28:41,160 --> 00:28:43,880
There's so much you don't know.

469
00:28:44,359 --> 00:28:45,119
Not just you.

470
00:28:45,680 --> 00:28:47,680
A lot of fathers in this world...

471
00:28:48,640 --> 00:28:50,599
don't really know their own children.

472
00:31:25,839 --> 00:31:27,160
The cases we discussed today

473
00:31:27,440 --> 00:31:29,640
are all real-world examples,

474
00:31:29,920 --> 00:31:31,599
and frankly, among the rare

475
00:31:31,599 --> 00:31:34,400
cautionary lessons made public.

476
00:31:36,480 --> 00:31:38,680
These security breaches

477
00:31:38,720 --> 00:31:39,880
involving military intelligence

478
00:31:39,880 --> 00:31:42,960
arose from unauthorized document sharing,

479
00:31:43,240 --> 00:31:43,880
as well as work secrets

480
00:31:43,880 --> 00:31:46,400
leaked through network transmissions.

481
00:31:46,759 --> 00:31:47,480
Confidentiality is no small matter.

482
00:31:47,480 --> 00:31:50,119
This time, we'll mostly have discussions.

483
00:31:50,240 --> 00:31:52,559
Later on, we will incorporate some

484
00:31:52,559 --> 00:31:54,039
scenario-based training.

485
00:31:58,200 --> 00:31:59,519
Feel free to take notes.

486
00:31:59,680 --> 00:32:02,039
For instance, handling classified files,

487
00:32:02,039 --> 00:32:03,680
the use of smart devices,

488
00:32:03,680 --> 00:32:05,480
and vetting information before disclosure.

489
00:32:08,480 --> 00:32:09,319
Chairman Xie.

490
00:32:09,599 --> 00:32:10,240
Hello, Chairman Xie.

491
00:32:11,000 --> 00:32:11,839
Hello, Chairman Xie.

492
00:32:13,279 --> 00:32:15,559
Have you wiped your hard drives?

493
00:32:15,799 --> 00:32:16,640
We'll do it right when we get upstairs.

494
00:32:17,880 --> 00:32:19,839
This confidentiality and security training

495
00:32:20,079 --> 00:32:21,240
has added a new requirement.

496
00:32:21,400 --> 00:32:22,440
Any drive used on business trips

497
00:32:22,440 --> 00:32:23,720
must be wiped clean immediately.

498
00:32:24,200 --> 00:32:26,079
So hand them in to the server room first

499
00:32:26,079 --> 00:32:26,880
for centralized processing.

500
00:32:27,240 --> 00:32:30,279
All your department's confidential records

501
00:32:30,279 --> 00:32:32,720
and data on all article contributors

502
00:32:32,880 --> 00:32:34,000
must be compiled into a report

503
00:32:34,000 --> 00:32:34,799
and submitted to me for signature.

504
00:32:35,039 --> 00:32:35,839
Understood.

505
00:32:36,559 --> 00:32:37,960
Handle this personally.

506
00:32:37,960 --> 00:32:38,640
The sooner, the better.

507
00:32:38,640 --> 00:32:39,519
Yes, understood.

508
00:32:39,960 --> 00:32:40,279
Chairman Xie.

509
00:32:40,279 --> 00:32:41,000
Goodbye, Chairman Xie.

510
00:32:41,000 --> 00:32:41,559
Okay.

511
00:32:41,720 --> 00:32:42,440
You two, follow me.

512
00:33:20,039 --> 00:33:20,519
Where to?

513
00:33:20,519 --> 00:33:22,000
3:30 to Quanzhou. One ticket.

514
00:33:29,000 --> 00:33:29,880
Passengers bound for Zhangzhou,

515
00:33:29,880 --> 00:33:31,119
please line up for ticket check.

516
00:33:47,799 --> 00:33:48,799
Is that you?

517
00:33:49,160 --> 00:33:50,039
Is this Reporter Yang?

518
00:33:50,519 --> 00:33:51,400
Professor Pan.

519
00:33:51,559 --> 00:33:52,559
What can I do for you?

520
00:33:52,759 --> 00:33:54,119
Are you free tonight?

521
00:33:54,279 --> 00:33:55,680
I have something to discuss with you.

522
00:33:57,000 --> 00:33:57,599
Sure.

523
00:34:00,559 --> 00:34:02,480
Excuse me, I'd like to return my ticket.

524
00:34:05,000 --> 00:34:06,640
Hello, welcome!

525
00:34:18,519 --> 00:34:19,119
Professor Pan.

526
00:34:20,280 --> 00:34:20,880
Please, have a seat.

527
00:34:25,119 --> 00:34:26,079
That woman

528
00:34:26,800 --> 00:34:29,000
has been pestering my son endlessly.

529
00:34:29,639 --> 00:34:30,400
Is there any way...?

530
00:34:31,239 --> 00:34:33,639
You mean make her disappear?

531
00:34:36,119 --> 00:34:37,159
Just getting her to leave is enough.

532
00:34:38,000 --> 00:34:38,840
Don't hurt her.

533
00:34:57,559 --> 00:34:58,400
So...

534
00:35:01,599 --> 00:35:02,800
this consulting role you mentioned,

535
00:35:03,559 --> 00:35:04,679
what would I actually be doing?

536
00:35:06,039 --> 00:35:07,960
When writing the Internal Reference,

537
00:35:07,960 --> 00:35:08,920
just provide a little nudge.

538
00:35:09,360 --> 00:35:11,440
Uncertainty is inherent in economics.

539
00:35:11,679 --> 00:35:13,880
However you steer it, left or right,

540
00:35:14,239 --> 00:35:15,440
there won't be any issue.

541
00:35:15,800 --> 00:35:18,239
This doesn't involve stealing secrets

542
00:35:18,559 --> 00:35:19,480
or passing intelligence.

543
00:35:19,920 --> 00:35:22,639
An investigation would yield no evidence.

544
00:35:23,079 --> 00:35:23,920
It's completely safe.

545
00:35:25,039 --> 00:35:27,480
You want me to influence state decisions.

546
00:35:30,320 --> 00:35:32,679
Offering policy advice is your job anyway.

547
00:35:32,920 --> 00:35:34,079
You have to speak up either way,

548
00:35:34,079 --> 00:35:35,400
so you can frame it however you like.

549
00:35:35,599 --> 00:35:37,679
Done right, it benefits the nation,

550
00:35:37,960 --> 00:35:38,960
as well as your family and children.

551
00:35:41,159 --> 00:35:42,440
I haven't ordered you a coffee yet.

552
00:35:42,840 --> 00:35:43,840
What will you have?

553
00:35:55,159 --> 00:35:56,280
I'm going to the restroom.

554
00:36:45,159 --> 00:36:46,559
A glass of water, please. Thank you.

555
00:36:46,840 --> 00:36:48,119
Certainly, ma'am. Just a moment.

556
00:36:51,400 --> 00:36:52,559
Here's your water.

557
00:37:29,000 --> 00:37:30,280
I trust you've been well.

558
00:37:43,960 --> 00:37:46,320
Find a payphone up ahead

559
00:37:46,320 --> 00:37:46,960
and pull over.

560
00:37:47,400 --> 00:37:48,000
All right.

561
00:38:09,440 --> 00:38:11,440
Leftover eggs and rice are in the fridge.

562
00:38:11,440 --> 00:38:13,440
Make some fried rice if you haven't eaten.

563
00:38:21,880 --> 00:38:22,800
What happened?

564
00:38:29,039 --> 00:38:30,880
Just that business with Xie Fengshi.

565
00:38:32,679 --> 00:38:33,960
The ministry has approved

566
00:38:34,079 --> 00:38:35,559
wiretapping his phone.

567
00:38:36,159 --> 00:38:37,320
Too many shots to give,

568
00:38:37,840 --> 00:38:39,000
too many holes to fill,

569
00:38:39,360 --> 00:38:40,519
too many messes to clean up.

570
00:38:44,559 --> 00:38:45,239
I'm just so tired.

571
00:38:48,760 --> 00:38:49,559
I'll go make the fried rice.

572
00:38:50,320 --> 00:38:51,599
I get what you meant now.

573
00:38:52,440 --> 00:38:53,320
About you and Qiu Tian.

574
00:38:55,440 --> 00:38:59,320
It's like watching someone

575
00:38:59,320 --> 00:39:00,639
plunge into a bottomless abyss,

576
00:39:00,920 --> 00:39:02,079
and being completely powerless to stop it.

577
00:39:02,920 --> 00:39:03,920
Xie Fengshi?

578
00:39:06,760 --> 00:39:07,559
His son.

579
00:39:25,199 --> 00:39:27,039
Get my son a green card.

580
00:39:27,239 --> 00:39:29,239
Send him to the US within a week.

581
00:39:30,199 --> 00:39:31,679
I want a house in Irvine,

582
00:39:31,679 --> 00:39:32,639
a car,

583
00:39:33,199 --> 00:39:36,119
and living expenses to ensure his dignity.

584
00:39:38,000 --> 00:39:38,880
At midnight tonight,

585
00:39:39,960 --> 00:39:41,199
log into your email again.

586
00:39:41,400 --> 00:39:42,800
I sent you an encrypted email.

587
00:39:43,199 --> 00:39:45,000
The password is my initials and birthday.

588
00:39:54,719 --> 00:39:55,480
Where are you?

589
00:39:55,679 --> 00:39:56,559
The police said

590
00:39:56,960 --> 00:39:58,960
someone tipped them off about the weed.

591
00:39:59,159 --> 00:40:00,800
It couldn't be anyone but Lin Kanshan.

592
00:40:00,920 --> 00:40:01,840
Listen to me.

593
00:40:01,840 --> 00:40:04,079
From now on, we need to be more careful.

594
00:40:04,320 --> 00:40:06,360
If he asks to meet, let me know.

595
00:40:06,360 --> 00:40:07,199
We'll go together.

596
00:40:07,719 --> 00:40:08,880
The school is still safe.

597
00:40:09,000 --> 00:40:10,079
Don't wander around for now.

598
00:40:10,199 --> 00:40:11,400
Once this blows over,

599
00:40:11,800 --> 00:40:12,679
I'll come find you.

600
00:40:15,239 --> 00:40:16,039
I know.

601
00:40:22,159 --> 00:40:24,400
Love always outweighs friendship.

602
00:40:26,440 --> 00:40:27,239
You see?

603
00:40:27,840 --> 00:40:29,440
He never trusted me.

604
00:40:31,000 --> 00:40:33,400
Why couldn't you be the one who leaked it?

605
00:40:36,320 --> 00:40:37,679
You'd think the same if you were him.

606
00:40:38,920 --> 00:40:39,719
It's only natural.

607
00:40:41,920 --> 00:40:42,760
So...

608
00:40:45,000 --> 00:40:47,239
if he finds out the pregnancy is fake,

609
00:40:47,239 --> 00:40:48,719
and the test report is fake too,

610
00:40:50,800 --> 00:40:51,800
what will he think?

611
00:40:55,239 --> 00:40:57,599
I'll arrange the hospital reports for you,

612
00:40:58,039 --> 00:40:59,679
both blood work and ultrasound.

613
00:41:02,440 --> 00:41:04,079
Giving up his parents for you,

614
00:41:04,679 --> 00:41:07,239
throwing away his career and his future,

615
00:41:07,960 --> 00:41:11,079
only to end up like this.

616
00:41:11,599 --> 00:41:12,639
Honestly,

617
00:41:13,480 --> 00:41:15,280
sometimes I dare not even think about it.

618
00:41:17,519 --> 00:41:18,320
Tell me,

619
00:41:20,960 --> 00:41:22,400
doing things like this all the time,

620
00:41:23,480 --> 00:41:24,760
will we go to hell for it?

621
00:41:35,320 --> 00:41:37,039
Are you mocking me,

622
00:41:37,039 --> 00:41:38,440
or mocking our superiors?

623
00:41:42,519 --> 00:41:43,920
I don't know either.

624
00:41:44,760 --> 00:41:46,480
Why am I telling you all this?

625
00:41:47,960 --> 00:41:51,320
Maybe you're the only one I can tell.

626
00:41:58,519 --> 00:42:02,039
I offered my heart in vain.

627
00:42:07,360 --> 00:42:08,519
Forget it, let's drop it.

628
00:42:11,679 --> 00:42:12,840
Have a safe trip.

629
00:42:15,199 --> 00:42:16,320
In three days,

630
00:42:16,800 --> 00:42:19,360
to Hong Kong, China, then back to Taipei.

631
00:42:21,440 --> 00:42:22,679
Even if we go to hell,

632
00:42:24,719 --> 00:42:26,679
our superiors will end up a level deeper.

633
00:42:36,719 --> 00:42:38,119
With them leading the way,

634
00:42:39,480 --> 00:42:40,880
could we move a little faster?

635
00:42:45,679 --> 00:42:46,880
What choice do we have if we refuse?

636
00:42:50,400 --> 00:42:51,400
You said last time

637
00:42:54,559 --> 00:42:57,440
that people in any other field can quit,

638
00:42:57,960 --> 00:42:58,960
but not us.

639
00:43:08,400 --> 00:43:09,199
I'm Oho Ou,

640
00:43:09,199 --> 00:43:10,800
inviting you to watch the TV series

641
00:43:10,800 --> 00:43:11,719
*Confrontation*.

642
00:43:11,840 --> 00:43:12,639
Let's turn ourselves in.

643
00:43:12,639 --> 00:43:14,400
To Guangzhou National Security Bureau.

644
00:43:14,719 --> 00:43:16,159
Will passenger Huang Ziyan

645
00:43:16,159 --> 00:43:18,519
please proceed to Gate 103 for boarding.

646
00:43:18,760 --> 00:43:19,480
In half an hour,

647
00:43:19,480 --> 00:43:21,320
Xie Xiaozhou's flight will touch down.

648
00:43:21,320 --> 00:43:22,480
Those hunting him are likely

649
00:43:22,480 --> 00:43:24,480
already waiting at the airport exit.

650
00:43:24,559 --> 00:43:26,199
We're racing against the enemy right now.

651
00:43:26,199 --> 00:43:27,199
You know what I mean.

652
00:43:27,400 --> 00:43:29,320
Once you make a deal with the Americans,

653
00:43:29,320 --> 00:43:32,199
there's no turning back from that mistake.

654
00:43:32,199 --> 00:43:33,960
I had only one choice back then:

655
00:43:34,119 --> 00:43:35,360
trade it

656
00:43:35,519 --> 00:43:37,719
to secure a future for Xiaozhou.
